tp://www.archeryhalloffame.com/inductee-page2.html)**[Contact Us](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/About%20us.html)********----------******[**Director**](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/Board%20of%20Directors.html)**s**\n\n_****_ _**# Dr. Paul Klopsteg **Class of 1976** **\\_Influence on the Sport\\_** # Notes of Interest * Archery scientist, author * Co-authored Archery: The Technical Side with Dr. C. N. Hickman and Forrest Nagler * Physicist and Research Engineer; Chief of Research/Development Section in General MacArthur's command in the Pacific Theatre of Operations during World War II * Developed methods and devices for covert use by secret agents behind enemy lines; later, Professor of Applied Science, Northwestern University * All recurve composite bows made today make use of his scientific findings * Chairman, Board of Governors, National Archery Association, 1935-39 * Recipient, National Archery Association's Thompson Medal of Honor, 1939 * Recipient, National Field Archery Association Compton Medal of Honor, 1947 \\_**![Image 2](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/images/Klopsteg/Klopsteg2.jpg) Fred Bear and Dr. Klopsteg at the 1976 Induction ![Image 3](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/images/Klopsteg/hof.jpg)**\\_**_![Image 4](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/images/Klopsteg/Klopsteg-1%20-%20Ye%20Sylvan%20Bk%20Pg%205%20.jpg) ![Image 5](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/images/Klopsteg/klopsteg3.jpg) ![Image 6](http://www.archeryhalloffame.com/images/Klopsteg/sleeping.jpg)\n\nCopyright: 2017 Archery Hall of Fame & Museum, Inc. Unauthorized use of images and content is strictly prohibited. - All Rights Reserved -Office: P.O. Box 558 North Main Street Union City, PA 16438 USA Phone: 1.814.392.8901 Email:[info@archeryhalloffame.org](mailto:info@archeryhalloffame.org)\n"
